Beatrix,<br />
<br />
You have found the disposition mapping and you are the third person to find=
 it independently.<br />
<br />
The legacy code set had four closing values, C-1 through C-4. C-4 meant clo=
sed on registrant undertaking. SENTRY has three closing values and no equiv=
alent of C-4, so at cutover every C-4 was written as C-2, closed no further=
 action, on the reasoning that neither is a referral. That is why 2012-0118=
 reads the way it does. The underlying EXAMTRAC extract still carries the o=
riginal value, and I have pulled it for you: 2012-0118 was closed C-4 on Oc=
tober 3, 2012.<br />
<br />
It is not confined to your matter. I ran the extract against the Philadelph=
ia legacy series and Delamere Quill's 2011-0417 is the same shape - C-4 in =
EXAMTRAC, C-2 in SENTRY, and a closing letter that recites corrective actio=
n. There are eleven others in this office alone.<br />
<br />
The change request is SENTRY-2214 and it was closed will-not-fix in 2016 as=
 low impact. I am reopening it with your example attached, because "low imp=
act" was always a statement about the migration budget and never a statemen=
t about the records.<br />
